SUMMARY:Educator Trek: Great Coharie River Paddling Tour for Educators
DESCRIPTION:  \n \nExplore North Carolina’s beautiful Coharie River. We will learn about the Riverkeepers restoration initiatives and hear directly from members of the Coharie Tribe about their experiences living along the river. Become familiar with one of North Carolina’s wild areas and connect with the long history of the people who call this land home. \nTransportation: Participants will ride with the group from Raleigh departing at 8:30am. Transportation will be in Museum vans or bus. \nCredit: 8 contact hours toward CEUs or Criteria II/III for North Carolina’s Environmental Education Certification Program \nRegistration: This program is full. Please join our waiting list below. \nThe full workshop fee is due when you register and payment is via credit card. Registration for most Educator Treks is on a first-come\, first-served basis. Treks fill quickly\, so register early! If when you attempt to register it is full\, please join our waiting list and we will notify you as soon as possible if a space opens for you! \nNote: We do not want cost to be a barrier for any educator. If the cost of this workshop would prevent your participation\, please reach out to Megan Davis.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/educator-trek-great-coharie-river-paddling-tour/
LOCATION:In the Field
CATEGORIES:Educator Treks,Educators,Environmental Conference Center,Trips,Workshops
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan%20Davis":MAILTO:megan.davis@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
